      "writtenOn": "2024-03-04T02:48:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the caller uses TetheringManager#registerTetheringEventCallback, the ITetheringEventCallback shouldn\u0027t be null. The only explanation I can think of is that the caller is using reflection to call ITetheringConnector#registerTetheringEventCallback directly. Having null protection seems like a good idea, but ITetheringConnector#registerTetheringEventCallback is a one-way binder. So what happens if we throw an exception from the one-way binder? I don\u0027t think the exception will reach the caller\u0027s process. In that case, throwing an exception is pointless.",
